==English==
{{wikipedia||''Tetris''}}
[[File:Typical Tetris Game.svg|thumb|right|A ''Tetris''-style game in progress.]]

===Etymology===
From {{uder|en|ru|Те́трис|}}, coined by the creator of the game, [[w:Alexey Pajitnov|Alexey Pajitnov]], from the Russian numerical prefix {{m|ru|тетра-||tetra-}} (as all of the game's pieces contain four segments) and {{m|ru|те́ннис||tennis}}, his favourite sport.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈtɛtɹɪs/|a=UK,US}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-Tetris.wav|a=Southern England}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# A puzzle [[video game]] in which [[falling]] [[tetromino]]es must be manipulated to form complete lines, which are then cleared from the grid.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2001|author=Matt O'Keefe|title=You Think You Hear|page=25
|passage=There is one nice moment in the music, but it's not the moment identified by the owner of the system, and one idiot goes so far as to gush, "This is better than '''Tetris'''!"}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2007|author=David Skibbins|title=The Star: A Tarot Card Mystery|page=147
|passage=From the kitchen the guy said, "I write science fiction. Or I'm trying to write. I've been staring at that screen for three days. You just interrupted a one-hour '''Tetris''' marathon. I need to talk to a real human being."}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2008|author=Daniel Radosh|title=Rapture Ready!: Adventures in the Parallel Universe of Christian Pop Culture|page=213
|passage={{...}}there were some other guys there who were into cosplay—that's costume play—and their thing was, they were dressed as '''Tetris''' blocks.}}
# {{lb|en|figuratively}} An endeavor involving rearranging things of different shape into a physical space.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=Clare Sudbery|title=The dying of delight|passage=Then I looked at the furniture. It was all a bit unimaginative, so I rearranged everything at a jaunty angle. When I returned to the cellar I was still playing '''Tetris''' with the cooker in my head.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2005|author=Jack Leonard|title=Bad Altitude
|passage=While I worked out a '''''Tetris'''''-like arrangement to get all of the leftovers into the oven, Phil's curiosity got the better of him.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2005|author=Rachel DeWoskin|title=Foreign Babes in Beijing: Behind the Scenes of a New China|page=134
|passage=When people spoke to me, the sounds of their words were '''Tetris''' shapes, falling. All I had to do was put each one in its bright, satisfying place.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2007|author=David Chinnery; Kurt William Keutzer|title=Closing the Power Gap between ASIC & custom|page=234
|passage=The '''tetris''' method does have some shortcomings, however. In placements produced by ''Feng Shui'', the cells are closely packed.}}

