===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|video games|by extension}} The act of clearing four lines at once (the maximum possible) in ''Tetris''.
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1990|title=Et cetera, Volumes 47-48
|passage=For some it's staying low on the play field, steadily advancing through the levels, for others its {{SIC}} trying to clear the board entirely or scoring an unprecedented number of '''tetrises'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1995|author=Kurt Driessens|chapter=Relational Reinforcement Learning|title=Recent Trends in Data Type Specification|page=276
|passage=See figure 3 for an example of a logical decision tree that indicates whether there is a possibility to score a '''tetris'''.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2003|author=Tandy Warnow; Binhai Zhu|title=Computing and combinatorics: 9th annual international conference
|passage=Maximizing the number of '''tetrises''' (the number of times that four rows are cleared in a Tetris game) is NP-complete.}}
#* {{quote-text|en|year=2007|author=Barbara Smith; Chad Yancey|title=Video Game Achievements and Unlockables
|passage=Score two '''Tetrises''' in two drops playing Marathon.}}

